write('live-padel-score-iphone/index.html', '''<!doctype html><html lang="en-GB"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Live Padel Score on iPhone with Live Activities | PadelWrist</title><meta name="description" content="Keep your current padel score visible on iPhone with PadelWrist Live Activities and Dynamic Island while scoring points from Apple Watch."><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large,max-snippet:-1"><link rel="canonical" href="https://padelwrist.com/live-padel-score-iphone/"><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.png"><meta property="og:site_name" content="PadelWrist"><meta property="og:title" content="Live Padel Score on iPhone | PadelWrist"><meta property="og:description" content="Live Activities and Dynamic Island keep your active padel match visible on supported iPhones while Apple Watch handles fast scoring."><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:url" content="https://padelwrist.com/live-padel-score-iphone/"><meta property="og:image" content="https://padelwrist.com/assets/padelwrist-social-card.png"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:title" content="Live Padel Score on iPhone | PadelWrist"><meta name="twitter:description" content="Keep the current score visible with Live Activities and Dynamic Island while scoring from Apple Watch."><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://padelwrist.com/assets/padelwrist-social-card.png"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebPage","name":"Live Padel Score on iPhone with Live Activities","url":"https://padelwrist.com/live-padel-score-iphone/","description":"How PadelWrist uses Live Activities and Dynamic Island to keep an active padel match visible on iPhone.","dateModified":"2026-09-01","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://padelwrist.com/#website"},"about":{"@id":"https://padelwrist.com/#app"},"inLanguage":"en-GB"}</script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/styles.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/launch.css"><script src="/assets/site.js" defer></script></head><body class="page-body"><a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header solid"><div class="shell nav-wrap"><a class="brand" href="/"><span class="brand-mark">PW</span><span>PADELWRIST</span></a><nav class="site-nav"><a href="/">Home</a><a href="/guides/">Guides</a><a href="/support/">Support</a></nav></div></header><main id="main" class="content-page shell"><div class="page-heading reveal"><p class="eyebrow">Live Activities · PadelWrist 1.4</p><h1>Keep the live padel score visible on iPhone.</h1><p>PadelWrist can keep your active match close at hand through Live Activities and Dynamic Island on supported iPhones, while Apple Watch remains the quickest place to record each point.</p></div><article class="guide-copy"><section class="reveal"><h2>Why a Live Activity helps during padel</h2><p>You should not have to keep reopening an app just to check the match state. A Live Activity gives the current match a persistent, glanceable place on iPhone so the score remains easier to follow between rallies or from courtside.</p></section><section class="reveal"><h2>Score on Apple Watch, follow on iPhone</h2><p>PadelWrist is designed around different roles for different devices. Apple Watch is built for the scoring interaction itself: one quick update after the rally. iPhone can then keep the active match visible without becoming the thing you have to hold throughout play.</p><p><a href="/apple-watch-padel-scoring/">See how Apple Watch scoring works →</a></p></section><section class="reveal"><h2>Dynamic Island on supported iPhones</h2><p>On iPhones that support Dynamic Island, the current match can remain visible in that system surface as part of the Live Activity experience. Availability and presentation depend on the iPhone model and iOS behaviour.</p></section><section class="reveal"><h2>Part of one match across your Apple devices</h2><p>The Live Activity is not a separate scoreboard you need to maintain. It is another view of the same active PadelWrist match, alongside the Apple Watch, iPhone and iPad experiences.</p></section><section class="reveal"><h2>After the match, switch from live score to Insights</h2><p>Once the match ends, the useful question changes from “what is the score?” to “what does this result tell me?”. Match History and the dedicated Insights tab take over with recent form, player analysis, trends and post-match milestones.</p><p><a href="/padel-player-statistics/">Explore Insights →</a></p></section><aside class="guide-cta reveal"><h2>Keep the match visible without keeping your phone in your hand.</h2><p>Download PadelWrist for Apple Watch, iPhone and iPad.</p><a class="feedback-link" data-app-store-cta href="https://apps.apple.com/gb/app/padelwrist/id6799725420" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View PadelWrist on the App Store</a></aside><nav class="related-guides reveal"><a href="/apple-watch-padel-scoring/">Apple Watch padel scoring →</a><a href="/padel-match-history/">Searchable Match History →</a><a href="/whats-new/">What's new in 1.4 →</a></nav></article></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="shell footer-grid"><div><a class="brand" href="/"><span class="brand-mark">PW</span><span>PADELWRIST</span></a></div><nav><a href="/guides/">Guides</a><a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a></nav><p>© <span data-year>2026</span> PadelWrist</p></div></footer></body></html>''')

